> A hand-checkable calculation

A direction with Fisher quadratic4 is rescaled by sqrt(2*.01/4), giving approximate KL.01. The source then evaluates actual KL and surrogate improvement in an explicit backtracking line search.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/trpo_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::vector<double>values{std::sqrt(2*.01/4),4*std::pow(std::sqrt(2*.01/4),2)/2};std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,values[i]);dm::nn::save_npz("build/trpo_worked.npz",{{"values",dm::nn::from_vector(values)}});std::vector<double>x(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);double low=std::min(0.,*std::min_element(values.begin(),values.end())),high=std::max(0.,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.end())),span=std::max(1.,high-low);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(x,values,"worked values",{37,99,235}).ylim(low-.05*span,high+.05*span).title("trpo worked calculation").x_label("Displayed coordinate").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/trpo_worked.svg");}
```
